# The host list names real machines on private networks - keep it local.
condor-host-list

# Shared submit fragment. It pins jobs to named machines, so it carries real
# hostnames for the same reason condor-host-list does. tools/sanitise.sh flags
# it on every run - it scans untracked-but-not-ignored files precisely because
# those are what a `git add .` would sweep in.
tools/pool-common.inc
# Command records, captured output, and staged helper scripts name real
# machines too. Sanitise before tracking any of it.
logs/
scripts/
*~

# Credentials - never track.
wifi.txt
*.psk
*secret*

# LaTeX build products. The sources in latex/ are tracked; the output is not.
latex/build/
*.pdf

# Job scratch and test runs. Working area, never tracked.
run/

# Branding is supplied at deploy time and lives only on the machine that serves
# it. The dashboard reads /var/lib/pool-web/www, a copy rather than a mount, so
# nothing on the site depends on this repository. Keeping a company mark in a
# public repo would buy nothing that tools/pool-web/README does not.
tools/pool-web/*.png
